==English==

===Verb===
{{infl|en|verb|head=to [[go]] [[against the grain]]}}

# {{idiomatic}} To [[defy]] [[convention]]; to do something in a manner that is [[unusual]] or [[out of the ordinary]].
#: ''His method certainly '''goes against the grain''', but it is unquestionably effective.''

====Translations====
{{trans-top|to defy convention}}
* Portuguese: [[ir contra a corrente]] (literally: to swim up against the current) OR [[nadar contra a maré]] (to swim up against the tide)
